# Build/dev artifacts — never needed inside the image.
.venv
.git
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Runtime state that must never ship baked into the image — a developer's
# container starts with a clean catalog/checkpoint DB, not this machine's.
beatroot.db
beatroot.checkpoints.db

# Secrets — the whole point is that the image needs none of these to boot.
.env

# Planning material and internal working notes. The `docs/diagrams` and the
# two documents the `/docs` page serves are copied EXPLICITLY in the
# Dockerfile — excluding `docs` wholesale is what left that page rendering a
# broken diagram and dead download links in every containerised run.
.sdd
docs/plans
docs/specs
docs/NOTES.md
docs/VIDEO_SCRIPT.md

# Generated eval output (not the eval source under src/beatroot/eval, nor
# the golden fixtures under eval/golden, nor eval/thresholds.yaml).
#
# `last_run.json` in particular MUST NOT ship. It is the artifact the
# `/evals` page renders, and baking it in meant the image carried whichever
# eval result happened to be on the builder's disk — so the page showed real
# scores that had nothing to do with this container, and a clone that built
# its own image showed none at all. An eval result is something you produce
# by running the suite, never something the image asserts on your behalf.
eval/synthetic
eval/healing
eval/last_run.json
eval/history
